Here is the general guidance from the council's outbuilding policy. A garden room usually doesn't need a planning application if it:

- is no more than 2.5 metres high,
- sits behind the front wall of the house,
- covers less than half of the garden.

Conservation areas and listed buildings are treated differently, so if your property is in either, you may need an application even if the room meets these limits.

